\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.1}{\ignorespaces Properties of the two datasets we study, at the headline $n{\le }256$ regime. Sequence identity is computed with MMseqs2\nobreakspace  {}\cite  {MMseqs2} (\texttt  {easy-search}, $\ge $30\% identity over $\ge $80\% alignment coverage).}}{60}{table.A.1}}
\newlabel{tab:setup-datasets}{{A.1}{60}{Properties of the two datasets we study, at the headline $n{\le }256$ regime. Sequence identity is computed with MMseqs2~\cite {MMseqs2} (\texttt {easy-search}, $\ge $30\% identity over $\ge $80\% alignment coverage)}{table.A.1}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.2}{\ignorespaces We read fold-level representation quality off CATH \emph  {Architecture}. Class is too coarse to discriminate, Topology too finely-bucketed to probe reliably. Class has 4 buckets (one at 55\%, baseline already 0.73); Topology has $\sim $1400 imbalanced buckets; Architecture sits between --- enough classes to be meaningful, enough examples per class to be learnable --- so CATH-A is our headline fold metric i the main text. (PDB-trained baseline, $n{\le }256$; ``baseline probe acc.'' is a linear probe on the un-aligned trunk, classifying validation chains by CATH code.)}}{61}{table.A.2}}
\newlabel{tab:setup-cath}{{A.2}{61}{We read fold-level representation quality off CATH \emph {Architecture}. Class is too coarse to discriminate, Topology too finely-bucketed to probe reliably. Class has 4 buckets (one at 55\%, baseline already 0.73); Topology has $\sim $1400 imbalanced buckets; Architecture sits between --- enough classes to be meaningful, enough examples per class to be learnable --- so CATH-A is our headline fold metric i the main text. (PDB-trained baseline, $n{\le }256$; ``baseline probe acc.'' is a linear probe on the un-aligned trunk, classifying validation chains by CATH code.)}{table.A.2}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {A.3}Leakage-controlled probe evaluation}{61}{section.A.3}}
